# Build-time values for production deploys. COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
# ── Why this file is in git ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This is a statically exported site: every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value below is baked
# into the public HTML at build time and served to every visitor. None of it is
# secret — it is the same phone number, address and GSTIN the site displays on
# every page and publishes in its JSON-LD.
#
# Keeping them here rather than only in the deploy dashboard means a fresh clone
# builds correctly with no out-of-band setup, and a misconfigured dashboard
# cannot silently publish the "+91 00000 00000" fallback to a live site.
#
# Precedence: .env.local wins over this file, so local overrides still work and
# a dashboard variable of the same name still wins over both in CI.
#
# NEVER add a secret here (API key, password, private token). Secrets belong in
# the Cloudflare dashboard, and the one write endpoint this site uses is kept
# there for exactly that reason — see NEXT_PUBLIC_ENQUIRY_ENDPOINT below.

NEXT_PUBLIC_PHONE="+91 7042658705"
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAIL="shreevinayakgases@gmail.com"

# Must match the Google Business Profile listing character-for-character.
# Local search ranking depends on this consistency.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADDRESS_STREET="Opp. CEL"
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADDRESS_LOCALITY="Sahibabad Town, Sahibabad"
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADDRESS_CITY="Ghaziabad"
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADDRESS_PIN="201005"

NEXT_PUBLIC_GSTIN="09ABWPK216P1ZQ"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://shreevinayakgases.in"

# NEXT_PUBLIC_ENQUIRY_ENDPOINT is deliberately absent.
#
# It is a write endpoint: anything that POSTs to it appends a row to the
# enquiries spreadsheet and sends an email. It already ships in the public JS
# bundle, so this is not a secret in the strict sense — but this repository is
# public, and a URL in a public repo is far easier to scrape at scale than one
# buried in a bundle. Set it in the Cloudflare dashboard instead.
#
# scripts/check-env.mjs fails the build if it is missing, so a deploy can never
# quietly ship a form that posts nowhere.
